From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Favre <ben@webdesign29.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:58:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Filaments: initialise machine candidate usage before copying

Why: Machine filament candidates leave their inherited usage enum uninitialised. Moving them into candidate vectors reads an invalid enum. Value-initialise all fields and use Hybrid for machine candidates whose model usage is not yet assigned.

Files: src/libslic3r/FilamentGroupUtils.cpp. Upstreamable: yes; reproduced by strict sanitizer golden slices and multi-nozzle integration tests.

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 src/libslic3r/FilamentGroupUtils.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/FilamentGroupUtils.cpp b/src/libslic3r/FilamentGroupUtils.cpp
index 9b5858d..4c1d66a 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/FilamentGroupUtils.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/FilamentGroupUtils.cpp
@@ -108,7 +108,8 @@ namespace FilamentGroupUtils
         for (size_t idx = 0; idx < filament_configs.size(); ++idx) {
             auto& arr = filament_configs[idx];
             for (auto& item : arr) {
-                MachineFilamentInfo temp;
+                MachineFilamentInfo temp{};
+                temp.usage_type = FilamentUsageType::Hybrid;
                 std::string type;
                 std::string color;
                 std::string tray_name;
